<main class="viewport" aria-label="Thesis presentation"><div class="stage-wrap"><div class="stage"><section class="slide title-slide" id="s1" data-seconds="30" data-chapter="Master’s thesis defense" data-title="Exploring and Improving Fault Localization in LLM Inference Engines" data-note="讲述重点｜本研究的问题是：只拿到 issue 与修复前仓库，如何把开发者实际修改的文件排到前面。开场直接给对象、输入和目标。

教授可能追问｜这和自动修复有什么不同？

答复依据与边界｜只定位文件，不生成补丁，也不证明唯一根因。英文开场可用：I study how to rank the developer’s fault location using only an issue report and its pre-fix repository."  aria-label="01: Exploring and Improving Fault Localization in LLM Inference Engines" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow"></div><h1>Exploring and Improving Fault Localization in LLM Inference Engines</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="title-layout"><div class="title-copy"><div class="title-rule"></div><div class="title-main">Exploring and Improving Fault Localization<br><span>in LLM Inference Engines</span></div><div class="author"><span><strong>Tianhao Gu</strong><span class="author-date">02.2026–08.2026</span></span><span>Software Engineering &amp; AI (SEAI)<br><span class="advisor">Examiner: Prof. Dr. Chunyang Chen<br>Supervisor: Dr. Mark Huasong Meng</span></span></div></div>
<div class="title-visual" aria-hidden="true"><div class="visual-label">FROM FAILURE TO FAULT LOCATION</div><div class="issue-chip"><span class="orange-dot"></span> <svg class="github-icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27.68 0 1.36.09 2 .27 1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.01 8.01 0 0 0 16 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8z"/></svg> Issue report from GitHub</div><div class="trace-line"></div><div class="repo-tree"><div class="tree-root">inference-engine /</div><div class="tree-line">├─ server /</div><div class="tree-line">├─ runner /</div><div class="tree-line">├─ backend /</div><div class="tree-target">└─ <b>CMakeLists.txt</b><span>←</span></div></div><div class="visual-bottom"></div></div></div>
</div>

<footer class="slide-footer"><span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide agenda-slide" id="s2-agenda" data-seconds="35" data-chapter="Presentation structure" data-title="Research background, three research questions, contributions, and discussion" data-note="讲述重点｜本页先交代报告结构：背景与挑战、问题与数据、方法评估、失败分析、ClueFL 与结论。" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">CONTENTS</div><h1>Outline</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="agenda-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h2>Research Background</h2><p>Why is fault localization in LLM inference engines important and challenging?</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h2>RQ1 — Are the existing Fault Localization (FL) methods feasible?</h2><p>IRFL vs LLM-agent-based FL</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h2>RQ2 — Why do LLM-agent-based methods fail in some cases?</h2><p>Are there recurring failure patterns?</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h2>RQ3 — How does ClueFL (our agent) improve the baselines?</h2><p>Can domain knowledge and the designed workflow address observed failure patterns?</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h2>Contribution and Discussion</h2></div></article></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>Outline · Exploring and Improving Fault Localization
 in LLM Inference Engines</span><span>03<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>

<section class="slide section-divider" id="part1" data-chapter="Part I" data-title="Part I: Research Background" data-note="讲述重点｜章节过渡页，进入第一部分：研究背景。" aria-label="Part I: Research Background" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="divider-copy"><div class="divider-eyebrow">PART I</div><div class="divider-title">Research <span>Background</span></div><div class="divider-rule"></div><p class="divider-sub">Why is fault localization in LLM inference engines important and challenging?</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>Part I · Research Background</span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide deployment-slide" id="s2-deployment" data-seconds="55" data-chapter="01 / Background" data-title="How is an LLM deployed?" data-note="讲述重点｜部署分为 engine setup、model conversion 和 inference/serving 三个阶段。推理引擎贯穿这三个阶段；因此这一层一个缺陷即可影响整个系统。引用 Liu et al. Figure 1。" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">01 / Background</div><h1>How is an LLM deployed?</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<figure class="paper-figure deployment-figure fragment"><img src="images/llm_deployment_workflow.png" alt="Workflow of LLM deployment: engine setup, model conversion, and inference or serving." draggable="false"><figcaption>Workflow of LLM deployment [1]</figcaption></figure>
<div class="deployment-phases fragment"><div><span>01</span><h2>Engine setup</h2><p>Install or compile the inference engine and verify hardware compatibility.</p></div><div><span>02</span><h2>Model conversion</h2><p>Convert, optimize, and package the model for the selected engine and environment.</p></div><div><span>03</span><h2>Inference / serving</h2><p>Load the model, process requests, and generate responses.</p></div></div>
<div class="highlight-callout fragment">Inference engines sit at the intersection of deployment, hardware, and runtime.</div>
<div class="highlight-callout fragment">A single bug in the LLM inference engine can cascade into unacceptable consequences across millions of LLM services.</div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span class="footnote-cite">[1] <a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09713v1#S2.F1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Liu et al. · Fig. 1 · Workflow of LLM deployment ↗</a></span><span>02<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide " id="s2" data-seconds="70" data-chapter="01 / Background" data-title="LLM inference engines have complex infrastructure." data-note="讲述重点｜先用手势沿原图的 Request Parser → Job Manager → Input Processor → Operators → Output Processor 讲一遍请求流，再指出 Resource Manager 与 Backend Adapter 如何跨越这条路径。核心信息是：推理引擎协调服务、模型执行、资源、后端和异构设备，因此其故障定位需要跨层追踪。最后连接下一页的症状—修复距离。

教授可能追问｜这张通用架构图是你的贡献吗？

答复依据与边界｜不是。这是 Liu et al. Fig. 2 的背景图，已标注来源。我的工作使用 Ollama 专属导航映射来指导文件定位；它与这张通用背景图不同。图中的测试/监控组件也不意味着本实验执行它们。"  aria-label="02: LLM inference engines have complex infrastructure" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">01 / Background</div><h1>LLM inference engines have complex infrastructure.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">

<div class="arc-layout">
<div class="architecture-visual"><figure class="paper-figure architecture-original"><button class="figure-zoom" data-figure="images/llm_inference_engine_arc.png" data-caption="Liu et al. · Architecture of LLM inference engine · Fig. 2" data-source="https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09713v1#S2.F2" aria-label="Enlarge LLM inference engine architecture"><img src="images/llm_inference_engine_arc.png" alt="LLM inference engine architecture: service and job configurations, model loader, request parser, job manager, input and output processors, operators, resource manager, backend adapter, platforms and devices." draggable="false"><span class="zoom-hint">↗ Enlarge architecture</span></button><figcaption>Architecture overview [1]</figcaption></figure><div class="architecture-intro"><p style="padding:16px;background:#f5f5f5;border:2px solid #333;border-radius:6px;margin:0;line-height:1.6;">The complex infrastructure coordinates request handling, model execution, resource management, backend adapters, and heterogeneous devices.</p></div></div>
<aside class="architecture-reading"><div class="architecture-cards"><div class="architecture-card"><span>Module structure</span>Interdependent modules across the serving stack<br><em style="font-size: 0.85em; color: #666;">→ in which module does the fault actually lie in?</em></div><div class="architecture-card"><span>Lifecycle scope</span>Spans setup, conversion, and LLM inference<br><em style="font-size: 0.85em; color: #666;">→ which phase is the starting point of the failure?</em></div></div></aside>
</div>

</div>

<footer class="slide-footer"><span class="footnote-cite">[1] <a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2506.09713v1#S2.F2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Liu et al. · Fig. 2 · Background figure</a></span><span>02<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide" id="s3-fl-apr" data-seconds="50" data-chapter="01 / Background" data-title="What is Fault Localization?" data-note="讲述重点｜先把 FL 放回 Automated Program Repair 的大背景里。APR 常见流程是输入问题描述、代码与测试，先做 fault localization，再让 patch generation 生成候选补丁，最后 validation 检查。这里特别强调：在本研究设定里没有 executable test suite，所以输入改为 issue report 和 codebase。随后给出文件级 FL 定义，并说明本研究关注的是 FL 这一步。" aria-label="04: What is Fault Localization?" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">01 / Background</div><h1>What is Fault Localization?</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="figure-split" style="grid-template-columns:minmax(0,820px) 1fr;gap:28px;align-items:stretch;">
<figure class="paper-figure" style="align-items:stretch;position:relative;margin:0;">
<div class="figure-zoom" style="padding:52px 16px 18px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:linear-gradient(180deg,#f7fafc 0%,#fff 100%);position:relative;overflow:hidden;">
<div style="position:absolute;left:18px;top:14px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.96);border:1px solid #cbd5e1;color:var(--navy);padding:8px 12px;border-radius:10px;font-size:15px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.25;text-align:left;box-shadow:0 5px 14px rgba(15,23,42,.08);">Workflow of Automated Program Repair (APR)</div>
<img src="images/apr_pipeline_raw.png" alt="Basic pipeline of automated program repair: inputs flow through fault localization, patch generation, and validation." draggable="false" style="max-height:420px;object-fit:contain;">
</div>
<div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:10px;margin-top:14px;padding-left:42px;color:#b42318;">
<div style="font-size:30px;line-height:1;font-weight:800;">&#8593;</div>
<div>
<div style="font-size:21px;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;">Issue report + codebase (our case)</div>
<div style="font-size:13px;line-height:1.35;margin-top:4px;">No executable test suite</div>
</div>
</div>
<figcaption style="margin-top:9px;font-size:11px;">APR pipeline [1]</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="metric-context" style="gap:36px;padding-top:0;justify-content:center;display:flex;flex-direction:column;">
<div style="padding:14px 16px;background:var(--pale);border-left:4px solid var(--blue);">
<span class="label" style="margin-bottom:8px;">FAULT LOCALIZATION</span>
<p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.4;color:var(--navy);">“Given the bug report and codebase, FL techniques identify buggy code elements (e.g., files or functions).” <span class="footnote" style="display:block;margin-top:7px;font-size:12px;">Definition from the 2025 FL survey [1].</span></p>
</div>
<div style="padding:14px 16px;background:var(--pale);border-left:4px solid var(--blue);">
<span class="label">Importance</span>
<h2 style="font-size:28px;margin:10px 0 8px;line-height:1.2;">Failure of FL can directly cause failure of the whole APR process.</h2>
<p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.45;">APR needs to localize the bug before patch generation and validation.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span class="footnote-cite">[1] Definition from 2505.19489 &middot; APR pipeline from Zhang et al. 2024, Fig. 1</span><span>04<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s3-fl-challenge" data-seconds="50" data-chapter="01 / Background" data-title="Why is fault localization hard for LLM inference engines?" data-note="讲述重点｜承上启下：解释为什么FL在这类系统上特别难。三点，均给出论文原文数字：①仓库规模与异质性——1,254个受跟踪文件、约32.4万行代码（23.8万Go+6.9万C/C+++1万TS），且逻辑还散布在配置、构建脚本、workflow、模型元数据等非源码文件里；②架构耦合导致症状与修复位置分离——28种root cause跨I/O、配置、功能、环境、资源管理，API可见症状可能要在别的层修复；③诊断证据有限——issue不一定带可执行失败测试、完整复现条件、日志或堆栈，复现还依赖特定模型/加速器/驱动/操作系统，静默或非确定性故障甚至没有pass/fail oracle。" aria-label="03: Why fault localization is hard for LLM inference engines" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">01 / Background</div><h1>Why is FL hard for LLM inference engines?</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="why-hard-grid">
<article class="why-hard-row"><div class="why-hard-stat"><span class="label">Scale</span><strong>1,254</strong><span>tracked files · 324k LOC</span></div><div class="why-hard-copy"><h2>The candidate space is too large for a single LLM context.</h2><p>The repository cannot be fed directly into one prompt, so file-level localization must first narrow the search space before detailed reasoning begins.</p></div></article>
<article class="why-hard-row"><div class="why-hard-stat"><span class="label">Heterogeneous bug types</span><strong>28</strong><span>root-cause categories <a class="cite-num" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.09713" target="_blank" rel="noopener">[1]</a></span></div><div class="why-hard-copy"><h2>Issues and fault locations can live in different layers.</h2><p>Failures span configuration, runtime, I/O, and functional logic, so the issue description often points to a visible symptom rather than the actual file that needs to be fixed.</p></div></article>
<article class="why-hard-row"><div class="why-hard-stat"><span class="label">Reproduction constraints</span><strong>0</strong><span>executable test suite</span></div><div class="why-hard-copy"><h2>Reliable reproduction evidence is often missing.</h2><p>Many cases depend on specific hardware, drivers, models, or deployment environments, and issues often lack failing tests, complete traces, or stable reproduction steps.</p></div></article>
</div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span class="footnote-cite"><span>[1] Liu et al., arXiv:2506.09713</span></span><span>03<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
</section><section class="slide " id="s6" data-seconds="35" data-chapter="01 / Background" data-title="Research questions." data-note="讲述重点｜快速讲三问之间的因果关系：先确认能否做，再定位失败机制，最后把机制转成方法并验证。不要逐字朗读。"  aria-label="05: Research questions." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">01 / Background</div><h1>Research questions.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="rq-grid rq-grid-full"><article><div class="rq-number">RQ1</div><p><strong>Feasibility Exploration —</strong> Despite the aforementioned challenges, are representative IR-based and LLM-agent-based approaches feasible for execution-free file-level localization of the issues in the LLM inference engines?</p><span class="rq-method">Assessment: baseline feasibility</span></article><article><div class="rq-number">RQ2</div><p><strong>Failure Explainability —</strong> Do LLM-agent localization failures in LLM inference engines reduce to a small set of recurring, identifiable pitfalls?</p><span class="rq-method">Analysis: recurring failure patterns</span></article><article><div class="rq-number">RQ3</div><p><strong>Domain-Specific Improvement —</strong> Can incorporating domain-specific knowledge and a designed workflow address observed failure patterns?</p><span class="rq-method">Method proposal: ClueFL</span></article></div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>04<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide outline-return" id="outline-1" data-chapter="Outline" data-title="Outline — up next: RQ1 Feasibility" data-note="讲述重点｜回到大纲，划掉Part I，指向RQ1。" aria-label="Outline — up next: RQ1 Feasibility" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
