<section class="slide section-divider" id="part2" data-chapter="Part II" data-title="Part II: RQ1 · Feasibility" data-note="讲述重点｜章节过渡页，进入第二部分：RQ1可行性。" aria-label="Part II: RQ1 · Feasibility" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="divider-copy"><div class="divider-eyebrow">PART II</div><div class="divider-title">RQ1 · <span>Feasibility</span></div><div class="divider-rule"></div><p class="divider-sub">Are the existing FL methods feasible?</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>Part II · RQ1 · Feasibility</span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide " id="s8a" data-seconds="20" data-chapter="02 / RQ1 · OllamaFLBench" data-title="Why Ollama as the studied inference engine?" data-note="讲述重点｜说明为什么选Ollama作研究对象：8.9M开发者的真实采用规模；代码库覆盖模型获取管理、API服务与请求编排、资源调度、推理runner、硬件后端、构建部署产物等推理引擎全流程环节；多语言（Go/C/C++/TypeScript）真实工程复杂度，不是玩具项目。" aria-label="06: Why Ollama as the studied inference engine?" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">02 / RQ1 · OllamaFLBench</div><h1>Why Ollama as the studied inference engine?</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="ollama-grid">
<article class="ollama-stat-card"><span class="label">ADOPTION</span><h2>Widely used in practice</h2><div class="fl-stat">8.9M<small>developers served</small></div><p>Ollama is a live, widely adopted inference engine rather than a toy benchmark or research prototype.</p></article>
<div class="ollama-right"><article class="ollama-card"><span class="label">FULL WORKFLOW COVERAGE</span><h2>It covers the whole inference-engine workflow.</h2><div class="ollama-list"><span>model acquisition</span><span>model management</span><span>API serving</span><span>request orchestration</span><span>resource-aware scheduling</span><span>inference runners</span><span>hardware backends</span><span>build and deployment artifacts</span></div></article><article class="ollama-card"><span class="label">REAL-WORLD ENGINEERING</span><h2>Its repository reflects production complexity.</h2><p><strong>Go</strong>, <strong>C/C++</strong>, and <strong>TypeScript</strong> coexist with configuration, build, and workflow files, which makes it a realistic study target for repository-scale fault localization.</p></article></div>
</div>
<div class="takeaway"><span>WHY OLLAMA</span><p>A representative real-world case study for fault localization in LLM inference engines, not a synthetic benchmark.</p></div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>05<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide " id="s8b" data-seconds="20" data-chapter="02 / RQ1 · OllamaFLBench" data-title="Three steps turn issue&#8211;PR history into the OllamaFLBench." data-note="讲述重点｜给出数据集构建的三步总览，再用后续三页分别展开：Issue Collection→Fault Location Identification→Manual Inspection，最终得到145个validated instances。" aria-label="07: Three steps turn issue-PR history into the OllamaFLBench." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">02 / RQ1 · OllamaFLBench</div><h1>Three steps turn issue&#8211;PR history into the OllamaFLBench.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="trajectory"><div class="traj-step"><span class="traj-num">1</span><h3>Issue Collection</h3><p>Mine closed, bug-labeled Ollama issues that were actually fixed by a merged pull request.</p></div><div class="traj-arrow">→</div><div class="traj-step"><span class="traj-num">2</span><h3>Fault Location Identification</h3><p>Reconstruct the pre-fix snapshot and derive the exact repair-location label from the accepted fix.</p></div><div class="traj-arrow">→</div><div class="traj-step"><span class="traj-num">3</span><h3>Manual Inspection</h3><p>Manually check every candidate so only clean, single-label instances remain.</p></div></div>

</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>06<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide " id="s8c" data-seconds="30" data-chapter="02 / RQ1 · OllamaFLBench" data-title="Step 1 &#8212; Issue collection." data-note="讲述重点｜Step 1如何收集：从Ollama仓库拿到已关闭且带bug标签的issue；只保留通过merged PR关闭的issue（fixes/closes/resolves #N），并确认该PR确实被合并；两个例外直接排除：①一个PR修了不止一个issue；②PR只新建文件（没有pre-fix版本可定位）。" aria-label="08: Step 1 - Issue collection." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">02 / RQ1 · OllamaFLBench</div><h1>Step 1 &#8212; Issue collection.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="step-grid">
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">COLLECT</span><h2>Start from Ollama's issue tracker</h2><p>Pull closed issues that carry a bug label from the public Ollama GitHub repository.</p></article>
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">CONFIRM THE FIX</span><h2>Keep only issues closed by a merged PR</h2><p>Retain issues closed via an explicit reference (<code>fixes #N</code>, <code>closes #N</code>, <code>resolves #N</code>) to a pull request, and confirm that PR was actually merged.</p></article>
</div>
<div class="label" style="margin-top:22px">TWO EXCLUSIONS</div>
<div class="constraints"><span>PR fixes more than one issue</span><span>PR only creates new files</span></div>
<div class="takeaway"><span>WHY EXCLUDE</span><p>A multi-issue PR cannot be mapped back to a single issue, and a newly created file has no pre-fix version to localize.</p></div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>07<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide " id="s8d" data-seconds="30" data-chapter="02 / RQ1 · OllamaFLBench" data-title="Step 2 &#8212; Fault-location identification." data-note="讲述重点｜Step 2如何定位：先重建fix合并前的pre-fix快照；抽取该PR改动的每一个文件记录，如果任何一条记录在pre-fix快照里找不到，整个候选直接排除（不是只删那条记录）；再清洗掉vendored/生成/构建产物，做issue与PR的一致性检查，最后只保留恰好剩一个合格修复位置的候选。" aria-label="09: Step 2 - Fault-location identification." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">02 / RQ1 · OllamaFLBench</div><h1>Step 2 &#8212; Fault-location identification.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="step-grid step-grid-linked">
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">GROUND TRUTH</span><h2>The developer's own patch defines the label</h2><p>The merged PR's patch is used as ground truth — it is what a real developer actually changed to fix the issue, not a guess or an approximation.</p></article>
<div class="traj-arrow">→</div>
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">AVOID AMBIGUITY</span><h2>Keep only a single ground-truth file<span class="formula-badge">GT = 1</span></h2><p>If the patch's repair location resolves to more than one plausible file, the candidate is dropped — every retained instance has exactly one ground-truth repair location.</p></article>
</div>
<div class="takeaway"><span>OUTPUT</span><p>Each surviving candidate has exactly one reachable, patch-derived ground-truth repair-location label.</p></div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>08<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide " id="s8e" data-seconds="25" data-chapter="02 / RQ1 · OllamaFLBench" data-title="Step 3 &#8212; Manual inspection." data-note="讲述重点｜Step 3人工核查：人工确认issue和PR描述的是同一个问题、不是表面提及；核实最终标签确实是修复改动的文件而不是讨论中提到的文件；通过后才计入最终145个实例，每个实例正好一个repair-location标签。" aria-label="10: Step 3 - Manual inspection." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">02 / RQ1 · OllamaFLBench</div><h1>Step 3 &#8212; Manual inspection.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="challenge-grid">
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">RELEVANCE</span><h2>Is the PR actually about the issue?</h2><p>Drop cases where the linked PR is unrelated or only mentions the issue in passing — a mislabeled link, not a real fix.</p></article>
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">BUG VS. FEATURE</span><h2>Is this really a bug?</h2><p>Drop issues that are feature requests or enhancements mistakenly tagged as bugs.</p></article>
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">INFORMATION LEAKAGE</span><h2>Does the issue leak the fix?</h2><p>Drop issues with too little diagnostic information to localize, or so much detail that they already reveal the repair location.</p></article>
</div>
<div class="label" style="margin-top:16px">AI-ASSISTED RECOVERY</div>
<div class="step-grid">
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">MISSED BUGS</span><h2>Bugs never labeled "bug"</h2><p>An LLM scans the repository for issues that describe real bugs but were never tagged with the bug label.</p></article>
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">UNLINKED FIXES</span><h2>Fixes GitHub never auto-linked</h2><p>An LLM finds PRs that fix a bug issue but reference it in a format GitHub does not recognize, so no automatic issue&#8211;PR link is created.</p></article>
</div>
<div class="takeaway"><span>RESULT</span><p>Manual and AI-assisted checks together keep OllamaFLBench clean and recover cases that label- and keyword-based mining alone would miss — 145 validated instances in total.</p></div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>09<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s4-fl" data-seconds="65" data-chapter="02 / RQ1 · Baselines" data-title="Overview of existing fault-localization techniques." data-note="讲述重点｜先按证据来源把现有FL方法分成五类：IRFL（文本/结构相似度检索）、LLM-based FL（单次prompt直接读issue/代码）、LLM-agent-based FL（自主探索仓库）、SBFL（测试覆盖谱）、MBFL（变异体杀死模式）。然后现场做排除：SBFL和MBFL都需要可执行、可通过/失败的测试套件，这个数据集只有pre-fix仓库和issue，没有可运行的oracle，所以排除；LLM-based FL把整个仓库或大段代码塞进单次prompt，超出上下文长度，工程可行性差，排除。剩下IRFL与LLM-agent-based FL是唯一在这个设置下可行、不需要新执行证据的方法，这也是本论文RQ1实际评估的两类方法。最后引出研究缺口句子。

教授可能追问｜为什么不做SBFL/MBFL的近似（比如用历史测试）？

答复依据与边界｜数据集只保留pre-fix快照与issue，没有维护中的可执行测试oracle；构造近似测试超出本论文范围，留作未来工作。" aria-label="10: Overview of existing fault-localization techniques." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">02 / RQ1 · Baselines</div><h1>Overview of existing fault-localization techniques.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="fl-landscape">
<div class="fl-grid">
<article class="fl-card excluded"><h2>LLM-based FL<span>e.g., LLMAO, AutoFL</span></h2><p>Feeds the bug report and large spans of source code directly into one LLM call to score suspicious files or lines.</p><span class="fl-cite"><a class="cite-num" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3597503.3623342" target="_blank" rel="noopener">[5]</a></span><div class="fl-verdict"><span class="fl-mark">✗</span> Excluded in this setting — a full repository exceeds the usable context budget for single-pass prompting.</div></article>
<article class="fl-card excluded"><h2>SBFL <span>/</span> MBFL</h2><div class="fl-sub"><strong>SBFL</strong><span>Correlates pass/fail test-coverage spectra with suspicious statements.</span></div><div class="fl-sub"><strong>MBFL</strong><span>Compares mutant-kill patterns between passing and failing tests.</span></div><span class="fl-cite"><a class="cite-num" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/1101908.1101949" target="_blank" rel="noopener">[6]</a> <a class="cite-num" href="https://doi.org/10.1002/stvr.1509" target="_blank" rel="noopener">[7]</a></span><div class="fl-verdict"><span class="fl-mark">✗</span> Excluded — requires an executable test suite</div></article>
<article class="fl-card kept"><h2>IRFL<span>Information-Retrieval Fault Localization</span></h2><p>Ranks repository files by text and structural similarity between the bug report and the source code — no execution needed.</p><span class="fl-cite"><a class="cite-num" href="https://doi.org/10.1109/ICSE.2012.6227210" target="_blank" rel="noopener">[1]</a> <a class="cite-num" href="https://doi.org/10.1109/ASE.2013.6693093" target="_blank" rel="noopener">[2]</a></span><div class="fl-verdict"><span class="fl-mark">✓</span> Feasible — repository text only</div></article>
<article class="fl-card kept"><h2>LLM-agent-based FL<span>e.g., SWE-agent, AutoCodeRover</span></h2><p>An LLM autonomously searches, opens, and reasons over the repository, then proposes candidate files from the issue alone.</p><span class="fl-cite"><a class="cite-num" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.15793" target="_blank" rel="noopener">[3]</a> <a class="cite-num" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3650212.3680384" target="_blank" rel="noopener">[4]</a></span><div class="fl-verdict"><span class="fl-mark">✓</span> Feasible — no execution required</div></article>
</div>

</div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span class="footnote-cite">[1] Zhou et al. 2012 &middot; [2] Saha et al. 2013 &middot; [3] Yang et al. 2024 &middot; [4] Zhang et al. 2024 &middot; [5] Wu et al. 2024 &middot; [6] Jones &amp; Harrold 2005 &middot; [7] Papadakis &amp; Le Traon 2012</span><span>10<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
<section class="slide " id="s7" data-seconds="55" data-chapter="02 / RQ1 · Baselines" data-title="Studied Baselines." data-note="讲述重点｜IR 用适配多语言仓库的文本与结构表示；SWE-agent 迭代收集证据。明确是本论文的 multilingual adaptations，而非声称直接运行原作者未修改的实现。IRFL 方法是确定性的：相同输入总是产生相同排序。LLM-agentic 方法（SWE-agent）每个 case 独立运行两次，取两次结果的平均值。

教授可能追问｜Baseline 比较是否公平？

答复依据与边界｜实例、预修复快照、候选范围与 scorer 一致。跨 backbone 配置并不 prompt-matched，因此结果解读限于配置；RQ3 则在每个 backbone 内匹配。"  aria-label="07: Studied Baselines." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">02 / RQ1 · Baselines</div><h1>Studied Baselines.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="method-grid fragment"><article class="method"><span class="label">IRFL representative methods</span><h2>BugLocator <span>/</span> BLUiR<span class="cite-num right">[2]</span></h2><div class="method-flow"><span>Issue + repository</span><b>↓</b><span>Text / structural similarity</span><b>↓</b><span>relevance score of repository files</span></div><p><strong>Strength</strong> Deterministic retrieval</p><p><strong>Challenge</strong> Failure–fault location vocabulary mismatch</p></article><article class="method agent"><span class="label">llm-agent-based FL representative method</span><h2>SWE-agent<span class="cite-num right">[4]</span></h2><p class="model-detail">GPT-5.2 / DeepSeek V4 Pro configurations</p><div class="method-flow"><span>Issue + repository</span><b>↓</b><span>Iterative inspection and reasoning</span><b>↓</b><span>relevance score of repository files</span></div><p><strong>Strength</strong> Semantic, multi-step exploration</p><p><strong>Challenge</strong> Computation and exploration failures</p></article></div>
<p class="footnote fragment">IRFL methods (BugLocator, BLUiR) are deterministic given the same input. LLM-agentic runs (SWE-agent) are executed twice per case, and the reported results are averaged over the two runs.</p>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>11<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s9" data-seconds="60" data-chapter="02 / RQ1 · Results" data-title="Fault-location ranking results." data-note="讲述重点｜先说Top-1是第一文件命中，Top-5是前五个文件覆盖，MRR@5反映前五的排序位置。再报94/145与129/145，把比例落到可理解的案例数。

教授可能追问｜是否有统计显著性或重复试验？

答复依据与边界｜没有足以估计run-to-run variance的重复运行。说 observed improvement 或 higher in these runs，不用 statistically significant。"  aria-label="08: Fault-location ranking results." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">02 / RQ1 · Results</div><h1>Fault-location ranking results.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<figure class="paper-figure results-table fragment"><button class="figure-zoom" data-figure="images/table4-4-effectiveness.svg" data-caption="Table 4.4 · Localization effectiveness · p. 27" data-page="37" aria-label="Enlarge: Original Table 4.4: Top-1, Top-3, Top-5 and MRR@5 for BugLocator, BLUiR and the two SWE-agent configurations."><img src="images/table4-4-effectiveness.svg" alt="Original Table 4.4: Top-1, Top-3, Top-5 and MRR@5 for BugLocator, BLUiR and the two SWE-agent configurations." draggable="false"><span class="zoom-hint">↗ Enlarge original</span></button><figcaption>Localization effectiveness [1]</figcaption></figure>
<p class="footnote fragment">Top-k: fault location appears in the first k predictions. MRR@5: mean reciprocal rank, scored zero beyond rank 5. ↓: gap from the column best.</p>
<div class="three-findings fragment">
<article><span class="finding-index">FINDING 1</span><h2>Feasible despite the challenges</h2><p>Even with the vocabulary-mismatch and exploration challenges noted above, both IRFL and LLM-agent-based methods are feasible for execution-free fault localization on OllamaFLBench.</p></article>
<article><span class="finding-index">FINDING 2</span><h2>Agents outperform IRFL</h2><p>Across the evaluated backbones, LLM-agent-based methods substantially outperform IRFL methods overall.</p></article>
<article><span class="finding-index">FINDING 3</span><h2>Room to improve</h2><p>Considerable room for improvement remains; understanding how requires analyzing per-case exploration trajectories.</p></article>
</div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span class="footnote-cite">[1] </span><span>12<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
