<section class="slide pattern-intro" id="s12ns" data-seconds="25" data-chapter="03 / RQ2 · Failure evidence" data-title="Failure pattern — non-source under-inspection" data-note="讲述重点｜先报出第三种失败模式：agent 看到非源码产物的引用却不打开。用 4/145 与 Case 103（docs/api.md）作引子，下一页再用 Table 4.6 给出 source vs non-source 的定量差距。" aria-label="09: Failure pattern — non-source under-inspection" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="pattern-card"><span class="pattern-eyebrow">Failure pattern</span><h1 class="pattern-title">Non-source<br><span>under-inspection</span></h1><p class="pattern-desc">Seeing a documentation or config reference is not the same as opening it — the repair file can sit in a linked artifact the agent never inspects.</p><span class="pattern-count">4 of 145 cases</span></div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>Failure pattern · Case 103</span><span>13<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide " id="s12" data-seconds="55" data-chapter="03 / RQ2 · Failure evidence" data-title="Top-5 ranking performance for non-source fault locations." data-note="讲述重点｜先交代112 source与33 non-source的扩展名分组，再指向GPT Top-5下降30.62pp。用该现象引出手工看trajectory的动机。

教授可能追问｜分组是否等同于失败模式？

答复依据与边界｜不是。定量分组按扩展名；non-source under-inspection机制还可涉及被分入可执行脚本组的构建/安装脚本。分组差距本身不能证明因果机制。"  aria-label="09: Top-5 ranking performance for non-source fault locations." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">03 / RQ2 · Failure evidence</div><h1>Top-5 ranking performance for non-source fault locations.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="artifact-strip fragment"><span class="artifact-tag">Configuration</span><span class="artifact-tag">Build specifications</span><span class="artifact-tag">Model metadata</span><span class="artifact-tag">Templates &amp; docs</span></div>
<figure class="paper-figure artifact-table fragment"><button class="figure-zoom" data-figure="images/table4-6-artifacts.svg" data-caption="Table 4.6 · Effectiveness by fault location artifact · p. 32" data-page="42" aria-label="Enlarge: Original Table 4.6: every evaluated configuration loses effectiveness on non-source fault locations compared with source code."><img src="images/table4-6-artifacts.svg" alt="Original Table 4.6: every evaluated configuration loses effectiveness on non-source fault locations compared with source code." draggable="false"><span class="zoom-hint">↗ Enlarge original</span></button><figcaption>Effectiveness by fault location artifact [1]</figcaption></figure>
<div class="evidence-note fragment"><strong>−30.62 pp</strong><p>GPT-5.2 agent’s Top-5 gap:<br><b>82.14% source → 51.52% non-source</b></p><span><b>112 source · 33 non-source</b><br>Inspect the archived failure trajectories.</span></div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span class="footnote-cite">[1] </span><span>14<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide pattern-intro" id="s12a" data-seconds="25" data-chapter="03 / RQ2 · Failure evidence" data-title="Failure pattern — evidence non-reachability" data-note="讲述重点｜先报出模式名称与占比，再用下一页的Case126具体trajectory来支持这个结论。" aria-label="10: Failure pattern — evidence non-reachability" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="pattern-card"><span class="pattern-eyebrow">Failure pattern</span><h1 class="pattern-title">Evidence<br><span>non-reachability</span></h1><p class="pattern-desc">A file that is never opened cannot be ranked — even when it sits right next to the code the agent does explore.</p><span class="pattern-count">5 of 145 cases</span></div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>Failure pattern 1 of 2</span><span>15<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide trajectory-slide" id="s12b" data-seconds="40" data-chapter="03 / RQ2 · Failure evidence" data-title="Both agents get stuck in the GPU-discovery branch." data-note="讲述重点｜带着观众逐步走一遍agent的探索路径：先看issue，再搜GPU相关代码，两个agent都停留在GPU分支，始终没打开真正的CPU启动文件。用轨迹本身说明遗漏，而不是直接下结论。" aria-label="11: Trajectory — Case 126, evidence non-reachability" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">03 / RQ2 · Case 126</div><h1>Both agents get stuck in the GPU-discovery branch.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="trajectory"><div class="traj-step"><span class="traj-num">1</span><h3>Reads the issue</h3><p>Windows startup fails on a machine with no GPU installed.</p></div><div class="traj-arrow">→</div><div class="traj-step"><span class="traj-num">2</span><h3>Searches GPU discovery code</h3><p>Opens <code>discover/gpu_cuda.go</code> and <code>discover/gpu_rocm.go</code> to check GPU-detection logic.</p></div><div class="traj-arrow">→</div><div class="traj-step"><span class="traj-num">3</span><h3>Follows GPU-related logs</h3><p>Both GPT-5.2 and DeepSeek keep re-reading GPU-branch files referenced in the crash log.</p></div><div class="traj-arrow">→</div><div class="traj-step traj-miss"><span class="traj-num">✕</span><h3>Never opens the CPU startup path</h3><p>The actual fault location <code>discover/cpu_windows.go</code> stays outside the explored context in both runs.</p></div></div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>Case 126 of 145 · both configurations rank the fix outside their Top-5</span><span>16<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide pattern-intro" id="s12e" data-seconds="25" data-chapter="03 / RQ2 · Failure evidence" data-title="Failure pattern — causal-chain truncation" data-note="讲述重点｜同样先报名称与占比，再用下一页的Case86具体trajectory来支持。" aria-label="12: Failure pattern — causal-chain truncation" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="pattern-card"><span class="pattern-eyebrow">Failure pattern</span><h1 class="pattern-title">Causal-chain<br><span>truncation</span></h1><p class="pattern-desc">When the fix crosses a language or process boundary, agents that stop exploring at that boundary miss it.</p><span class="pattern-count">7 of 145 cases</span></div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>Failure pattern 2 of 2</span><span>17<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide trajectory-slide" id="s12c" data-seconds="40" data-chapter="03 / RQ2 · Failure evidence" data-title="GPT-5.2 stops one hop before the native producer." data-note="讲述重点｜同样逐步走trajectory：GPT-5.2在Go侧扫描逻辑处停止，从未跨越语言边界进入native producer；DeepSeek越过这条边界并命中。先讲行为，再在下一页点出"causal-chain truncation"这个名字。" aria-label="13: Trajectory — Case 86, causal-chain truncation" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">03 / RQ2 · Case 86</div><h1>GPT-5.2 stops one hop before the native producer.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="trajectory"><div class="traj-step"><span class="traj-num">1</span><h3>Reads the issue</h3><p>A streaming response is missing its final token.</p></div><div class="traj-arrow">→</div><div class="traj-step"><span class="traj-num">2</span><h3>Opens the Go-side scanning loop</h3><p>Follows the token-stream parser inside the Go server package.</p></div><div class="traj-arrow">→</div><div class="traj-step"><span class="traj-num">3</span><h3>Confirms the Go logic looks complete</h3><p>The scanning loop appears to read every chunk correctly.</p></div><div class="traj-arrow">→</div><div class="traj-step traj-miss"><span class="traj-num">✕</span><h3>Stops at the language boundary</h3><p>Never crosses into the native producer <code>llm/ext_server/server.cpp</code>, where the final token is actually dropped. DeepSeek V4 Pro continues past this boundary and ranks the file first.</p></div></div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>Case 86 of 145 · GPT-5.2 misses the fix; DeepSeek V4 Pro finds it</span><span>18<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide " id="s13" data-seconds="45" data-chapter="03 / RQ2 · Failure patterns" data-title="Three recurring failure mechanisms." data-note="讲述重点｜逐个讲具体遗漏：Case126忽略CPU启动文件；Case86在Go到native producer边界停止；Case103看到文档链接却不打开。每类都讲观察到的动作和遗漏，而不是泛泛说LLM不理解。

教授可能追问｜谁做了编码，有没有一致性检验、频率统计？

答复依据与边界｜论文报告了手工trajectory分析与案例，但没有在这里提供编码者一致性或各类频率。不要临场编造kappa、双人标注或分布。三类机制可以重叠。"  aria-label="14: Three recurring failure mechanisms." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">03 / RQ2 · Failure patterns</div><h1>Three recurring failure mechanisms.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">

<div class="case-grid">
<article><span class="label">CASE 126 · 5 OF 145 CASES</span><h2>Evidence<br>non-reachability</h2><p class="case-lesson">A neighboring path stays outside the explored context.</p></article>
<article><span class="label">CASE 86 · 7 OF 145 CASES</span><h2>Causal-chain<br>truncation</h2><p class="case-lesson">The relevant chain crosses a language and process boundary.</p></article>
<article><span class="label">CASE 103 · 4 OF 145 CASES</span><h2>Non-source<br>under-inspection</h2><p class="case-lesson">Seeing a reference is not the same as inspecting its evidence.</p></article>
</div>

</div>

<footer class="slide-footer"><span>19<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section>
