<section class="slide section-divider" id="part4" data-chapter="Part IV" data-title="Part IV: RQ3 · Improvement (ClueFL)" data-note="讲述重点｜章节过渡页，进入第四部分：RQ3领域知识改进。" aria-label="Part IV: RQ3 · Improvement (ClueFL)" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="divider-copy"><div class="divider-eyebrow">PART IV</div><div class="divider-title">RQ3 · <span>Improvement</span></div><div class="divider-rule"></div><p class="divider-sub">How does ClueFL (our agent) improve baselines?</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>Part IV · RQ3 · Improvement</span></footer>
</section>
<section class="slide " id="s15" data-seconds="80" data-chapter="04 / RQ3 · Framework" data-title="ClueFL uses repository evidence to rank candidate files." data-note="讲述重点｜解释原图和下方操作规则：非零层分数决定源码探索范围；非源码文件做完整检查；用deps/pkg_summary/func控制读取粒度；最后每个文件给相关性分数和证据理由。

教授可能追问｜层分数和文件分数怎么校准，排零的层会不会错过？

答复依据与边界｜分数是LLM判断，不是校准概率。层分数为零会限制后续源码搜索，是潜在遗漏风险。k只决定最后读取多少排名，不改变探索流程；最终返回全部非零候选。"  aria-label="16: ClueFL uses repository evidence to rank candidate files." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">04 / RQ3 · Framework</div><h1>ClueFL uses repository evidence to rank candidate files.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<figure class="paper-figure framework-figure framework-operational fragment"><button class="figure-zoom" data-figure="images/fig5-1-cluefl.svg" data-caption="Fig. 5.1 · Original ClueFL framework · p. 39" data-page="49" aria-label="Enlarge: Original Figure 5.1: ClueFL combines project-specific knowledge, historical retrieval and root-cause expansion, then non-source inspection and repository navigation, followed by relevance ranking."><img src="images/fig5-1-cluefl.svg" alt="Original Figure 5.1: ClueFL combines project-specific knowledge, historical retrieval and root-cause expansion, then non-source inspection and repository navigation, followed by relevance ranking." draggable="false"><span class="zoom-hint">↗ Enlarge original</span></button><figcaption>ClueFL framework [1]</figcaption></figure>
<div class="operating-rules fragment"><div><span class="label">01 / SELECT SEARCH LAYERS</span><p>Retain layers with a non-zero<br>suspiciousness score.</p></div><div><span class="label">02 / COLLECT EVIDENCE</span><p>Inspect non-source artifacts;<br><code>deps</code> · <code>pkg_summary</code> · <code>func</code></p></div><div><span class="label">03 / RANK FILES</span><p>Relevance score + justification;<br>return all non-zero candidates.</p></div></div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span class="footnote-cite">[1] </span><span>21<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s16" data-seconds="80" data-chapter="04 / RQ3 · Results" data-title="ClueFL improves early ranking, especially with layer knowledge." data-note="讲述重点｜先报净增案例11和4，再说对应7.59pp与2.76pp。GPT覆盖也提升，DeepSeek Top-5不变，改善集中在前排优先级。

教授可能追问｜是否是更多工具、更多信息而不是领域知识在起作用？

答复依据与边界｜主比较评估完整配置：指导、历史、artifact策略和导航一起变。不能把全增益归于单一组件；下一页消融提供组件敏感性证据。"  aria-label="17: Effect of domain guidance on fault-location ranking." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">04 / RQ3 · Results</div><h1>Effect of domain guidance on fault-location ranking.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="gain-grid fragment"><div><span class="label">GPT-5.2 · TOP-1</span><strong>+7.59 <small>pp</small></strong><p>51.03% → 58.62% <span>74 → 85 cases</span></p></div><div><span class="label">DEEPSEEK V4 PRO · TOP-1</span><strong>+2.76 <small>pp</small></strong><p>64.83% → 67.59% <span>94 → 98 cases</span></p></div></div>
<figure class="paper-figure cluefl-table fragment"><button class="figure-zoom" data-figure="images/table5-2-cluefl.svg" data-caption="Table 5.2 · Matched baseline vs. ClueFL · p. 44" data-page="54" aria-label="Enlarge: Original Table 5.2: matched SWE-agent and ClueFL comparisons. GPT-5.2 improves across all cutoffs; DeepSeek improves Top-1 and Top-3 while Top-5 stays at 88.97%."><img src="images/table5-2-cluefl.svg" alt="Original Table 5.2: matched SWE-agent and ClueFL comparisons. GPT-5.2 improves across all cutoffs; DeepSeek improves Top-1 and Top-3 while Top-5 stays at 88.97%." draggable="false"><span class="zoom-hint">↗ Enlarge original</span></button><figcaption>Baseline vs. ClueFL comparison [1]</figcaption></figure>
<p class="footnote fragment">Within each pair: same backbone, issues, pre-fix snapshots, and scorer. Guidance + exploration workflow change together. One run per instance.</p>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span class="footnote-cite">[1] </span><span>22<span class="footer-total"> / 24</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s17" data-seconds="65" data-chapter="04 / RQ3 · Component ablation" data-title="Effect of removing domain guidance." data-note="讲述重点｜把消融作为贡献证据，解释每次去掉一个组件、其他保留。两个backbone都对layer knowledge移除最敏感；不要把整张表逐格读出来。

教授可能追问｜消融是否证明8层架构是唯一原因？

答复依据与边界｜不证明。消融差值包含组件交互、不可相加，每配置每issue只有一次运行。观察到的模式支持该设计，但需要重复实验评估稳定性。"  aria-label="18: Effect of removing domain guidance." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">04 / RQ3 · Component ablation</div><h1>Effect of removing domain guidance.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<figure class="paper-figure ablation-table fragment"><button class="figure-zoom" data-figure="images/table5-4-ablation.svg" data-caption="Table 5.4 · Leave-one-component-out ablation · p. 47" data-page="57" aria-label="Enlarge: Ablation results for both backbones; removing layer knowledge has the largest observed Top-1 decline."><img src="images/table5-4-ablation.svg" alt="Ablation results for both backbones; removing layer knowledge has the largest observed Top-1 decline." draggable="false"><span class="zoom-hint">↗ Enlarge original</span></button><figcaption>Leave-one-component-out ablation [1]</figcaption></figure>
<div class="inline-insights fragment"><p><b>−4.14 pp</b> without layer knowledge · GPT-5.2</p><p><b>−2.07 pp</b> without layer knowledge · DeepSeek</p></div>

</div>
