</section><section class="slide " id="s21" data-chapter="Backup / Success overlap" data-title="Improvement does not mean strict superset coverage." data-note="讲述重点｜分别解释新增成功与baseline独有成功，净改善不是成功集合严格包含。

教授可能追问｜为什么提高了还会退步？

答复依据与边界｜模型探索是随机的，加入指导也会改变搜索选择。GPT新增15、失去4，DeepSeek新增10、失去6；这只是归档运行的交集事实，尚未估计逐实例稳定性。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B03: Improvement does not mean strict superset coverage." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Success overlap</div><h1>Improvement does not mean strict superset coverage.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><figure class="paper-figure overlap-figure fragment"><button class="figure-zoom" data-figure="images/fig5-2-overlap.svg" data-caption="Fig. 5.2 · Baseline–ClueFL Top-1 intersections · p. 45" data-page="55" aria-label="Enlarge: Original Figure 5.2: GPT-5.2 baseline-only 4, shared 70, ClueFL-only 15; DeepSeek baseline-only 6, shared 88, ClueFL-only 10."><img src="images/fig5-2-overlap.svg" alt="Original Figure 5.2: GPT-5.2 baseline-only 4, shared 70, ClueFL-only 15; DeepSeek baseline-only 6, shared 88, ClueFL-only 10." draggable="false"><span class="zoom-hint">↗ Enlarge original</span></button><figcaption>Baseline–ClueFL Top-1 intersections [1]</figcaption></figure><div class="inline-insights fragment"><p><b>GPT-5.2:</b> 15 newly solved; 4 baseline-only.</p><p><b>DeepSeek:</b> 10 newly solved; 6 baseline-only.</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span class="footnote-cite">[1] </span><span>BACKUP · B03<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s22" data-chapter="Backup / Experimental controls" data-title="What is held fixed—and what changes?" data-note="讲述重点｜用原表逐项区分fixed与changed。历史只允许目标快照的祖先修复；对照在每个backbone内部进行。

教授可能追问｜公平比较还有哪些没有完全控制？

答复依据与边界｜无法控制随机种子，只有单次归档运行；完整ClueFL包中多个设计一起变化；跨模型prompt/endpoint也不统一。离线架构映射在所有issue中固定，并非每个历史快照都重建。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B04: What is held fixed—and what changes?" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Experimental controls</div><h1>What is held fixed—and what changes?</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<figure class="paper-figure control-table fragment"><button class="figure-zoom" data-figure="images/table5-1-controls.svg" data-caption="Table 5.1 · Controlled settings for the RQ3 comparison · p. 44" data-page="54" aria-label="Enlarge: Original table of fixed settings and intended differences between generic SWE-agent and ClueFL."><img src="images/table5-1-controls.svg" alt="Original table of fixed settings and intended differences between generic SWE-agent and ClueFL." draggable="false"><span class="zoom-hint">↗ Enlarge original</span></button><figcaption>Controlled settings for RQ3 comparison [1]</figcaption></figure>
<div class="protocol-notes fragment"><div><span class="label">HISTORY BOUNDARY</span><p>Only fixes ancestral to each target pre-fix snapshot; exclude the target fix and later changes.</p></div><div><span class="label">INTERPRETATION</span><p>Estimate the full ClueFL configuration change within each backbone. Individual components are probed by ablation.</p></div></div>

</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span class="footnote-cite">[1] </span><span>BACKUP · B04<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s23" data-chapter="Backup / Artifact analysis" data-title="ClueFL’s gains are not uniform across artifacts." data-note="讲述重点｜直面负结果：DeepSeek非源码Top-1从54.55%到51.52%，Top-5也下降；GPT两类均改善。

教授可能追问｜领域引导为什么没有普遍改善？

答复依据与边界｜论文结果不支持普遍改善。非源码仅33例，观察提示artifact与配置存在交互，但具体归因需更多运行和针对性分析，不能编造机制或显著性。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B05: ClueFL’s gains are not uniform across artifacts." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Artifact analysis</div><h1>ClueFL’s gains are not uniform across artifacts.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><figure class="paper-figure ablation-table fragment"><button class="figure-zoom" data-figure="images/table5-3-artifacts.svg" data-caption="Table 5.3 · Matched results by artifact type · p. 46" data-page="56" aria-label="Enlarge: Original Table 5.3: ClueFL improves GPT-5.2 source and non-source results but DeepSeek non-source Top-1 decreases from 54.55% to 51.52%."><img src="images/table5-3-artifacts.svg" alt="Original Table 5.3: ClueFL improves GPT-5.2 source and non-source results but DeepSeek non-source Top-1 decreases from 54.55% to 51.52%." draggable="false"><span class="zoom-hint">↗ Enlarge original</span></button><figcaption>Matched results by artifact type [1]</figcaption></figure><div class="inline-insights fragment"><p><b>112</b> source-code cases</p><p><b>33</b> non-source cases</p><p><b>−3.03 pp</b> DeepSeek non-source Top-1</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span class="footnote-cite">[1] </span><span>BACKUP · B05<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s24" data-chapter="Backup / Metrics" data-title="How are Top-k and MRR@5 defined, and why is the cutoff five?" data-note="讲述重点｜Top-k是修复文件出现在前k位的比例；MRR@5是前五名内首次命中位次的倒数均值，未命中记为0。cutoff=5参考Kochhar等对386名开发者的调查：73.58%把前五个元素当作可接受的最小检查范围，超过80%只在故障元素进入前五时才认为定位成功；也与AutoFL、SoapFL、FlexFL、DEVLoRe等近期研究一致。

教授可能追问｜为什么不报告Top-10或更长尾的结果？

答复依据与边界｜论文结论明确限定在前五名内的早期排序有效性，不刻画第五名之后的表现；k=5是有先例支撑的实践阈值，不是为了让结果好看而事后选择的cutoff。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B06: How Top-k and MRR@5 are defined, and why cut off at five." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Metrics</div><h1>How are Top-k and MRR@5 defined, and why is the cutoff five?</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="challenge-grid">
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">TOP-K ACCURACY</span><h2>Share within the first k</h2><p>Proportion of instances where the repair file appears in the first k ranked positions, for k = 1, 3, 5.</p><span class="fl-cite">Reported at Top-1, Top-3, Top-5.</span></article>
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">MRR@5</span><h2>Reciprocal rank, capped</h2><p>1 / rank of the first correct match within the top five; scored 0 if the repair file never appears there.</p><span class="fl-cite">Rewards earlier placement, not just presence.</span></article>
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">WHY CUTOFF = 5</span><h2>A practitioner-grounded bound</h2><p>73.58% of 386 developers treat five elements as their minimum inspection scope; &gt;80% call a session successful only within the top five.</p><span class="fl-cite">Kochhar et al.; consistent with AutoFL / SoapFL / FlexFL / DEVLoRe.</span></article>
</div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B06<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s25" data-chapter="Backup / Threats to validity" data-title="Construct, internal, and external validity threats." data-note="讲述重点｜三类威胁逐一讲：construct—用开发者实际改动的文件作为唯一标签，但其他文件也可能是有效修复；internal—预训练数据污染（GPT-5.2知识截止2025-08-31，与数据集时间窗口有重叠）以及agent不确定性（无可控随机种子，每例仅一次归档运行）；external—仅在Ollama单一仓库上评估，未覆盖vLLM、llama.cpp、TensorRT-LLM等其他推理引擎。

教授可能追问｜污染问题能否验证或排除？

答复依据与边界｜无法完全排除；论文只是坦诚披露这一风险边界，未做额外的污染检测实验。DeepSeek V4 Pro的训练语料和精确知识截止日期未公开，同样无法排除。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B07: Construct, internal, and external validity threats." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Threats to validity</div><h1>Construct, internal, and external validity threats.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="challenge-grid">
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">CONSTRUCT</span><h2>One label per fix</h2><p>Ground truth is the file the developer patch modifies. A valid fix could plausibly touch a different file — a known limitation of file-level FL.</p></article>
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">INTERNAL</span><h2>Contamination &amp; nondeterminism</h2><p>GPT-5.2's knowledge cutoff (31 Aug 2025) overlaps the OllamaFLBench window; no controllable random seed, one archived run per instance.</p></article>
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">EXTERNAL</span><h2>Ollama only</h2><p>Evaluated exclusively on Ollama. Other engines (vLLM, llama.cpp, TensorRT-LLM) may differ in architecture and development trajectory.</p></article>
</div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B07<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s26" data-chapter="Backup / Positioning" data-title="Why is ClueFL not directly benchmarked against LocAgent, GraphLocator, and similar tools?" data-note="讲述重点｜先承认repository-scale LLM exploration、图检索、领域推理并非本论文首创（LocAgent、CoSIL、OrcaLoca、GraphLocator、ARISE等已单独展示过）。缺口在于：没有工作在同一execution-free、file-ranking协议下，针对推理引擎的历史bug，评估这一整套组合——引擎专属操作模型、时序正确的快照、以及源码与非源码目标并存。ClueFL是有界新颖性声明：组合已有要素填补这一评估空白，而不是发明全新的单一算法。

教授可能追问｜那有没有和这些工具直接对比过？

答复依据与边界｜没有在本论文中直接复现对比；这些工具的协议、数据集和目标构件类型各不相同，直接移植超出本论文范围，留作未来工作。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B08: Why ClueFL is not directly benchmarked against LocAgent, GraphLocator, and similar tools." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Positioning</div><h1>Why is ClueFL not directly benchmarked against LocAgent, GraphLocator, and similar tools?</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="protocol-notes fragment"><div><span class="label">ALREADY EXISTS, SEPARATELY</span><p>Adaptive retrieval, graph traversal, iterative exploration, causal framing, domain-specific reasoning, and bounded reranking — each already demonstrated by LocAgent, CoSIL, OrcaLoca, GraphLocator, ARISE, and others.</p></div><div><span class="label">THE UNTESTED COMBINATION</span><p>An execution-free localizer with an inference-engine-specific operational model, a temporally correct snapshot, and eligible source + non-source targets — evaluated under one matched, historical-bug protocol.</p></div></div>
<div class="inline-insights fragment"><p><b>Bounded novelty:</b> ClueFL combines existing ingredients to fill this unstudied evaluation gap, not a claim of a new algorithmic primitive.</p></div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B08<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s27" data-chapter="Backup / Future work" data-title="Four directions raised by this thesis's own limitations." data-note="讲述重点｜按论文顺序讲四个方向：(1) root-cause-to-fix-strategy知识，用预测的根因缩小候选层/文件范围；(2) 跨引擎与跨backbone评估，构建vLLM、llama.cpp、TensorRT-LLM等的对照数据集；(3) 重复运行评估稳定性与效率分布（token、耗时、成本）；(4) 面向Ollama维护者的用户研究，验证ClueFL能否实际缩短修复时间、提高修复准确率。

教授可能追问｜你认为这四个方向里最优先做哪个？

答复依据与边界｜论文没有给这四个方向排优先级；可以说明个人判断，但要讲清楚这是我个人观点而非论文结论。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B09: Four directions raised by this thesis's own limitations." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Future work</div><h1></h1></header>
<div class="slide-body">
<div class="challenge-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)">
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">KNOWLEDGE</span><h2>Root-cause → fix-strategy</h2><p>Map predicted root causes to fix strategies to further narrow candidate layers and files.</p></article>
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">GENERALIZATION</span><h2>Cross-engine &amp; cross-backbone</h2><p>Build comparable OllamaFLBench variants for vLLM, llama.cpp, TensorRT-LLM; evaluate more backbones.</p></article>
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">ROBUSTNESS</span><h2>Repeated-run evaluation</h2><p>Repeat each configuration to quantify ranking stability and cost/latency variance.</p></article>
<article class="fl-card"><span class="label">IMPACT</span><h2>User study</h2><p>Have Ollama maintainers use ClueFL on real tasks to measure repair-time and accuracy gains.</p></article>
</div>
</div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B09<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s28" data-chapter="Backup / Baselines" data-title="Three baselines: two deterministic retrievers, one iterative agent." data-note="讲述重点｜BugLocator和BLUiR都是确定性one-shot排序：前者用rVSM加历史相似SimiScore（0.2权重），后者把issue拆成title/body两个查询字段，对代码结构字段做BM25并求和，两者都有多语言适配。SWE-agent则是迭代式：可以list目录、搜文本、读文件片段，最后必须输出有序文件列表，不做补丁生成。

教授可能追问｜这些baseline是原作者的实现吗？

答复依据与边界｜不是，是论文作者针对Ollama多语言仓库做的语言无关重实现，保留两种方法的核心评分设计，而非作者的可执行原始工件。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B10: Three baselines: two deterministic retrievers, one iterative agent." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Baselines</div><h1>Three baselines: two deterministic retrievers, one iterative agent.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="challenge-grid"><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">BUGLOCATOR</span><h2>rVSM + SimiScore</h2><p>Score(f) = 0.8·N(rVSM) + 0.2·N(SimiScore); historical fixes must predate the target issue.</p><span class="fl-cite">Deterministic, one run per issue.</span></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">BLUIR</span><h2>Structured BM25</h2><p>Title/body query fields × type/function/identifier/comment code fields, summed BM25 (k1=1.2, b=0.75); plain-text fallback for unsupported artifacts.</p><span class="fl-cite">Deterministic, one run per issue.</span></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">SWE-AGENT</span><h2>Iterative exploration</h2><p>Localization-only adaptation: list/search/read repository, then output a ranked file list — no patch generation, no execution.</p><span class="fl-cite">Stochastic, one archived run per issue.</span></article></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B10<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s29" data-chapter="Backup / Backbone selection" data-title="Why were GPT-5.2 and DeepSeek V4 Pro selected as the two SWE-agent backbones?" data-note="讲述重点｜选择一个闭源、一个开源模型，代表两种可获得的模型家族，而不是宣称覆盖所有模型。最终配对同时受API成本约束。两者是两个具有代表性的agent配置，不是对模型家族性能的全面估计，也不宣称在写作时仍是最强模型。

教授可能追问｜为什么不多测几个模型？

答复依据与边界｜受限于API成本与工程时间；论文明确将此作为局限，未来工作提出跨backbone评估作为方向之一。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B11: Why GPT-5.2 and DeepSeek V4 Pro as the two SWE-agent backbones." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Backbone selection</div><h1>Why were GPT-5.2 and DeepSeek V4 Pro selected as the two SWE-agent backbones?</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">DIVERSITY GOAL</span><p>One proprietary reasoning model (GPT-5.2) and one open-weight model (DeepSeek V4 Pro) — diversity in backbone family, not single-provider reliance.</p></div><div><span class="label">PRACTICAL CONSTRAINT</span><p>The final pairing was also constrained by API cost; each stochastic configuration is represented by one archived run per instance.</p></div></div><div class="inline-insights"><p><b>Not a claim:</b> that either backbone is the strongest model available at the time of writing.</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B11<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s30" data-chapter="Backup / Computational cost" data-title="IR retrieval is cheap and deterministic; agent exploration is costly but stronger." data-note="讲述重点｜BugLocator平均3.88秒/issue，BLUiR因多语言解析要107.39秒，都没有模型推理或API开销。GPT-5.2平均20.81步、约248,732 token、71.26秒、每issue约0.1532美元；DeepSeek V4 Pro探索更深，52.57步、约306万token、277.13秒，但按当时计费反而更便宜，约0.0599美元。这是效果与成本的明确权衡，而非模型能力的全面排名。

教授可能追问｜能不能用更便宜的方式达到同样效果？

答复依据与边界｜论文没有测试折中方案；IR方法可以通过持久化索引进一步降低边际延迟，但仍然远弱于agent的排序效果。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B12: IR retrieval is cheap and deterministic; agent exploration is costly but stronger." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Computational cost</div><h1>IR retrieval is cheap and deterministic; agent exploration is costly but stronger.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="challenge-grid"><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">BUGLOCATOR</span><h2>3.88 s / issue</h2><p>No model inference, no API cost. No persistent index across issues.</p></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">BLUIR</span><h2>107.39 s / issue</h2><p>Slower due to multilingual structural parsing, not an inherent property of the retrieval design.</p></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">SWE-AGENT</span><h2>GPT-5.2 vs DeepSeek</h2><p>GPT-5.2: 20.81 steps, ~248.7K tokens, 71.26 s, US$0.1532. DeepSeek V4 Pro: 52.57 steps, ~3.06M tokens, 277.13 s, US$0.0599.</p><span class="fl-cite">DeepSeek: more exploration, lower per-issue cost.</span></article></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B12<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s31" data-chapter="Backup / Oracle union" data-title="Aggregate Top-1 hides which instances each configuration actually solves." data-note="讲述重点｜GPT-5.2单独解决36例，BugLocator和BLUiR各自只有3例和1例独有，三者都同意的只有19例，三者oracle union到80例（55.17%）。两个SWE-agent配置重叠更强：都命中68例，DeepSeek独有26例，GPT独有6例，union到100例（68.97%），比DeepSeek单独还多4.14个百分点。四配置全部合并也只到103例（71.03%），42例始终无人命中。

教授可能追问｜能不能做一个集成模型？

答复依据与边界｜这些union数字假设完美的事后选择，是互补覆盖的上界，不是可部署的集成系统的预期表现。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B13: Aggregate Top-1 hides which instances each configuration actually solves." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Oracle union</div><h1>Aggregate Top-1 hides which instances each configuration actually solves.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">IR + GPT-5.2</span><p>36 uniquely solved by GPT-5.2 alone; 3 by BugLocator; 1 by BLUiR; 19 agreed by all three. Oracle union: 80/145 (55.17%).</p></div><div><span class="label">TWO AGENT CONFIGS</span><p>68 shared; DeepSeek +26 unique; GPT-5.2 +6 unique; 45 unsolved by either. Union: 100/145 (68.97%).</p></div></div><div class="inline-insights"><p><b>All four combined:</b> 103/145 (71.03%); 42 cases remain unsolved by any configuration.</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B13<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s32" data-chapter="Backup / Artifact-type gap (RQ1)" data-title="Every RQ1 approach is markedly worse when the repair location is non-source." data-note="讲述重点｜四种方法在non-source（33例）上全部下降，Top-5降幅从16.86到30.62个百分点不等，SWE-agent GPT-5.2降幅最大（30.62pp）。举例PR 9773，ROCm在gfx1151上损坏，正确修复位置是CMakePresets.json，BugLocator和BLUiR评分都是0，因为issue的GPU架构、驱动词汇和这份JSON文件的字面内容毫无重叠。

教授可能追问｜这是不是意味着IR方法完全不适合非源码文件？

答复依据与边界｜不是绝对失效，是词汇/结构证据不足导致的系统性弱点；agent方法虽然更强但同样显著下降，说明这是任务本身的难点而非某个方法特有的缺陷。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B14: Every RQ1 approach is markedly worse when the repair location is non-source." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Artifact-type gap (RQ1)</div><h1>Every RQ1 approach is markedly worse when the repair location is non-source.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="challenge-grid"><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">BUGLOCATOR</span><h2>Top-5 −24.16 pp</h2><p>54.46% (source) → 30.30% (non-source).</p></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">BLUIR</span><h2>Top-5 −16.86 pp</h2><p>56.25% (source) → 39.39% (non-source).</p></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">SWE-AGENT (GPT-5.2)</span><h2>Top-5 −30.62 pp</h2><p>82.14% (source) → 51.52% (non-source) — the largest observed drop.</p><span class="fl-cite">DeepSeek V4 Pro: 92.86% → 75.76% (−17.10 pp).</span></article></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B14<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s33" data-chapter="Backup / Case study · semantic reasoning" data-title="Case 107: iterative reasoning finds progress.go with no lexical cue at all." data-note="讲述重点｜PR 9079，issue只说SSH会话里CLI进度条闪烁，没有文件名、函数名或错误字符串。BugLocator/BLUiR都排不进Top-5，因为报告和progress/progress.go的字面重叠只有display这类通用词。两个SWE-agent配置都把它排第一：推理出终端渲染相关的症状指向进度条渲染器，即使没有直接词汇线索也能命中。

教授可能追问｜这说明IR方法完全没用吗？

答复依据与边界｜不是，IR在有词汇重叠时仍然有效且零成本；这个案例只是说明纯文本匹配在语义/因果推理场景下的边界。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B15: Case 107: iterative reasoning finds progress.go with no lexical cue at all." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Case study · semantic reasoning</div><h1>Case 107: iterative reasoning finds progress.go with no lexical cue at all.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">SYMPTOM</span><p>“CLI progress display flickers during pull over SSH” — no file name, function name, or error string in the report.</p></div><div><span class="label">OUTCOME</span><p>BugLocator/BLUiR fail to rank progress/progress.go in Top-5. Both SWE-agent configurations rank it 1st by reasoning that a rendering symptom implicates the progress-bar renderer.</p></div></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B15<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s34" data-chapter="Backup / Case study · evidence reachability" data-title="Case 126: strong local evidence can crowd out a neighboring repair location." data-note="讲述重点｜无GPU的Windows机器上出现大量GPU-discovery日志，两个agent都被引导进discover/runner.go、调度器、runner生命周期和CUDA后端初始化，但都没有打开discover/cpu_windows.go——真正的修复位置。这不是随机搜索失败，而是显著证据把搜索收窄得太厉害，相邻的启动路径根本没进入上下文。

教授可能追问｜这说明repo越大就一定越难定位吗？

答复依据与边界｜论文明确说这不是单纯的仓库规模问题，而是证据分配问题：规模和架构分散让这种问题更严重，但根因是agent没有跟踪哪些部署阶段/相邻子系统尚未探索。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B16: Case 126: strong local evidence can crowd out a neighboring repair location." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Case study · evidence reachability</div><h1>Case 126: strong local evidence can crowd out a neighboring repair location.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">WHAT HAPPENED</span><p>Long GPU-discovery logs from a GPU-less Windows machine drew both agents into discover/runner.go, the scheduler, and CUDA backend init.</p></div><div><span class="label">WHAT WAS MISSED</span><p>Neither agent opened discover/cpu_windows.go, where the accepted repair corrected the Windows CPU-discovery path.</p></div></div><div class="inline-insights"><p><b>Lesson:</b> a coverage-allocation problem, not proof that scale alone causes failure — track unexplored neighboring subsystems instead of assuming coverage from more actions in one subtree.</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B16<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s35" data-chapter="Backup / Case study · causal-chain truncation" data-title="Case 86: GPT-5.2 stops at the Go/native boundary; DeepSeek crosses it." data-note="讲述重点｜流式响应丢失最后一个token的问题，GPT-5.2沿server/routes.go、llm/server.go、api/client.go追踪，把问题归因于Go侧的scanning和流排序，但从未跨入native的响应生成器，结果是miss。DeepSeek继续深入llm/ext_server/server.cpp，检查了token和最终响应路径，第一名命中正确文件。

教授可能追问｜是不是GPT-5.2能力更弱？

答复依据与边界｜论文没有做这个归因；只是描述性观察，说明期望的行为不是简单地在一层里"挖得更深"，而是要跨越语言/进程边界、找出状态最先变得无效的位置，并在终止搜索前比较竞争层假设。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B17: Case 86: GPT-5.2 stops at the Go/native boundary; DeepSeek crosses it." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Case study · causal-chain truncation</div><h1>Case 86: GPT-5.2 stops at the Go/native boundary; DeepSeek crosses it.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">GPT-5.2 (miss)</span><p>Follows server/routes.go → llm/server.go → api/client.go; attributes the bug to Go-side scanning/ordering; never crosses into the native producer.</p></div><div><span class="label">DEEPSEEK V4 PRO (hit)</span><p>Continues into llm/ext_server/server.cpp, inspects the token/final-response path, and ranks the accepted repair location first.</p></div></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B17<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s36" data-chapter="Backup / ClueFL toolbox" data-title="Three purpose-built tools replace unrestricted source dumping." data-note="讲述重点｜deps查上下游依赖，帮助跨包/跨层追踪因果关系；pkg_summary返回文件摘要、imports、类型和函数签名而不含完整源码，用更低的上下文成本定位候选文件/函数；func取出指定Go或C/C++函数的实现，做针对性检查。仍保留grep/find/sed等通用命令做词法搜索或覆盖专用工具未覆盖的构件。

教授可能追问｜这些工具是不是针对Ollama写死的？

答复依据与边界｜工具面向Ollama的Go为主、Go/C/C++架构定制，论文明确说这是仓库特定的框架构件，属于第5章引入的内容，不作为通用背景声称。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B18: Three purpose-built tools replace unrestricted source dumping." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / ClueFL toolbox</div><h1>Three purpose-built tools replace unrestricted source dumping.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="challenge-grid"><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">deps &lt;package&gt;</span><h2>Cross-layer causal tracing</h2><p>Retrieves recorded upstream and downstream dependencies of a package.</p></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">pkg_summary &lt;package&gt;</span><h2>Low-cost candidate narrowing</h2><p>File summaries, imports, types, and function signatures — no full source dump.</p></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">func &lt;file&gt; &lt;fn&gt;</span><h2>Targeted evidence</h2><p></p></article></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B18<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s37" data-chapter="Backup / ClueFL × artifact type" data-title="ClueFL narrows the source/non-source gap for GPT-5.2, but not for DeepSeek." data-note="讲述重点｜GPT-5.2上，ClueFL在source和non-source两个子集所有指标都提升，Top-5 gap从30.62pp收窄到26.89pp，符合"鼓励搜索非源码构件"的设计目标。DeepSeek V4 Pro上则不均匀：source全面提升，但non-source（仅33例）里Top-1/Top-5/MRR@5各因1个case而下降3.03个百分点，gap反而从17.10扩大到21.02pp——因为DeepSeek的non-source baseline本来就已经很强（75.76% Top-5），改进空间有限。

教授可能追问｜这算不算ClueFL的负面结果？

答复依据与边界｜论文诚实报告这一点：ClueFL的收益并非在所有artifact类型和backbone上都均匀，33例的小样本下单个case的变化就有3.03pp，不能过度解读为系统性退步。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B19: ClueFL narrows the source/non-source gap for GPT-5.2, but not for DeepSeek." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / ClueFL × artifact type</div><h1>ClueFL narrows the source/non-source gap for GPT-5.2, but not for DeepSeek.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">GPT-5.2</span><p>Gains at every metric on both subsets; source–non-source Top-5 gap narrows from 30.62 pp to 26.89 pp.</p></div><div><span class="label">DEEPSEEK V4 PRO</span><p>Source code improves throughout; non-source (33 cases) is mixed — Top-1/Top-5/MRR@5 each fall by one case, widening the gap to 21.02 pp.</p></div></div><div class="inline-insights"><p><b>Not uniform:</b> ClueFL's benefit depends on both artifact type and backbone, not a guaranteed improvement everywhere.</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B19<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s38" data-chapter="Backup / Case study · historical retrieval" data-title="PR 13445: a near-duplicate past fix redirects the search away from tokenization." data-note="讲述重点｜Gemma 3升级后输出乱码，含特殊token文本。SWE-agent baseline锁定tokenization假设，排model.go、tokenizer_spm.go等最高，正确文件model_text.go没进前十。ClueFL检索到标题几乎相同的历史issue，其确认修复正好是model_text.go，另一相关历史issue也指向同一文件，于是ClueFL第一名命中，并把原因归于滑窗与缓存attention逻辑而非tokenization。

教授可能追问｜历史检索会不会只是记住了同一个bug？

答复依据与边界｜历史修复只作为弱先验，agent仍需结合当前仓库证据判断；论文强调这是search heuristic而非确定性证据，因为相似症状在推理引擎里可能对应不同根因。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B20: PR 13445: a near-duplicate past fix redirects the search away from tokenization." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Case study · historical retrieval</div><h1>PR 13445: a near-duplicate past fix redirects the search away from tokenization.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">SWE-AGENT BASELINE</span><p></p></div><div><span class="label">CLUEFL</span><p>Retrieves a near-duplicate historical issue whose confirmed fix touched model_text.go, ranking it first and attributing the bug to sliding-window/cached-attention logic.</p></div></div><div class="inline-insights"><p><b>Why it matters:</b> most useful when the symptom is compatible with more than one plausible subsystem.</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B20<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s39" data-chapter="Backup / Case study · root-cause expansion" data-title="PR 6905: the checklist adds an environment-mismatch hypothesis the baseline never considers." data-note="讲述重点｜Windows GUI启动的Ollama比CLI启动明显更慢。SWE-agent baseline锁定调度假设，怀疑tray图标的LockOSThread和消息循环饿死其他goroutine，把真正文件llm/llm_windows.go排到第六。ClueFL在root-cause checklist提示下额外考虑环境/运行时不匹配类别，假设GUI进程继承了不同的Windows进程环境，改变了runner子进程的生成方式和加载的CUDA库，这直接指向llm/llm_windows.go，排名第一。

教授可能追问｜28类根因checklist会不会让agent机械枚举？

答复依据与边界｜论文明确说checklist不是要求逐类核对，而是提供系统化的诊断空间，让agent在收敛到单一解释前先考虑多个可能机制。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B21: PR 6905: the checklist adds an environment-mismatch hypothesis the baseline never considers." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Case study · root-cause expansion</div><h1></h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">SWE-AGENT BASELINE</span><p></p></div><div><span class="label">CLUEFL</span><p>The checklist adds an environment/runtime-mismatch category alongside scheduling, pointing directly at llm/llm_windows.go, which is ranked 1st.</p></div></div><div class="inline-insights"><p><b>Mechanism:</b> adds an alternative causal category early enough to be verified against evidence, rather than replacing the agent's own reasoning.</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B21<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s40" data-chapter="Backup / Case study · repository navigation" data-title="PR 5121: deps + pkg_summary + func turn a vague suspicion into a checkable function-level claim." data-note="讲述重点｜DeepSeek-V2-Lite加载时CUDA OOM并伴随GGML shape断言。两个agent都怀疑内存估算子系统（memory.go、server.go），但baseline只能泛泛地把ggml.go排得很靠后，理由只是它提供EstimateGPULayers用到的元数据。ClueFL用deps确认scheduler和runtime层的依赖边界，用pkg_summary列出memory.go/server.go/ggml.go候选，再用func直接读EstimateGPULayers和GraphSize的实现，发现GraphSize对deepseek2架构没有分支、静默返回0，导致显存估算走了错误的兜底路径。ClueFL把ggml.go排第二，并给出可验证的函数级机制。

教授可能追问｜为什么不直接读整个文件，需要这些专用工具？

答复依据与边界｜直接读完整源码会用大量上下文并可能截断输出；专用工具用更低上下文成本定位候选文件/函数，这是沿用SWE-agent的专用工具设计原则，针对Ollama的Go/C/C++架构定制。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B22: PR 5121: deps + pkg_summary + func turn a vague suspicion into a checkable function-level claim." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Case study · repository navigation</div><h1>PR 5121: deps + pkg_summary + func turn a vague suspicion into a checkable function-level claim.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">SWE-AGENT BASELINE</span><p>Ranks llm/ggml.go far down the list, reasoning only that it holds metadata used by EstimateGPULayers.</p></div><div><span class="label">CLUEFL</span><p>deps confirms the scheduler/runtime boundary; pkg_summary shortlists three files; func reveals GraphSize silently returns 0 for the deepseek2 architecture — ClueFL ranks ggml.go 2nd with a verifiable mechanism.</p></div></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B22<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s41" data-chapter="Backup / OllamaFLBench" data-title="Eight stages turn raw issue–PR history into 145 single-label instances." data-note="讲述重点｜从ollama/ollama公开历史挖掘issue-PR关联并确认已合并（1-2）；恢复完整边界并抽取修复前后所有改动文件，此时尚未做构件过滤（3）；要求每条改动记录都能在tracked、可读的pre-fix文件集中定位，否则整条候选排除（4）；清洗仅移除vendored依赖、生成文件和构建产物，保留测试/脚本等只要它们确实是修复目标（5-6）；做issue-PR-修复一致性检查，只保留恰好一个合格标签的实例（6-7）；最终得到145个实例（8）。

教授可能追问｜为什么允许测试文件作为标签？

答复依据与边界｜执行自由协议只禁止运行测试，不禁止把维护中的测试源码当作候选排名目标；例如server/routes_test.go是合法修复位置。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B23: Eight stages turn raw issue–PR history into 145 single-label instances." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / OllamaFLBench</div><h1>Eight stages turn raw issue–PR history into 145 single-label instances.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="challenge-grid"><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">MINING &amp; CONFIRMATION</span><h2>Stages 1–2</h2><p>Mine issue↔PR links from closed bug-labeled issues and explicit closing references; confirm the change was merged.</p></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">SNAPSHOT &amp; REACHABILITY</span><h2>Stages 3–4</h2><p>Extract every changed-file record with no filtering yet; exclude the whole candidate if any record is unreachable in the tracked pre-fix tree.</p></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">CLEANING &amp; FINAL LABEL</span><h2>Stages 5–8</h2><p>Remove vendored/generated artifacts, check issue–PR consistency, retain only |G_i| = 1 → 145 final instances.</p></article></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B23<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s42" data-chapter="Backup / Contributions summary" data-title="Three contributions, kept distinct from any claim of a general-purpose repair tool." data-note="讲述重点｜(1) 第一个系统评估issue引导、执行自由、文件级定位在LLM推理引擎bug上的研究，比较IR方法与LLM-agent方法在效果、成本、backbone和失败行为上的差异；(2) 一个可复用的145例Ollama issue-fix评估数据集，含pre-fix快照和单文件修复标签，公开发布；(3) ClueFL框架，证明外部知识和精心设计的工作流能提升LLM推理引擎bug的文件排序效果。

教授可能追问｜这三个贡献里你认为哪个最重要？

答复依据与边界｜论文没有排序；可以说数据集是可复用的基础设施贡献，ClueFL是方法贡献，评估本身填补了此前没人系统做过的空白——三者互相支撑，非彼此独立。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B24: Three contributions, kept distinct from any claim of a general-purpose repair tool." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Contributions summary</div><h1>Three contributions, kept distinct from any claim of a general-purpose repair tool.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="challenge-grid"><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">EVALUATION</span><h2>First systematic study</h2><p>Compares IR-based and LLM-agent-based file localization for LLM inference-engine bugs under one execution-free protocol.</p></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">OllamaFLBench</span><h2>145 validated instances</h2><p>Repository-derived Ollama issue–fix pairs with pre-fix snapshots and single-file repair labels, released publicly.</p></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">FRAMEWORK</span><h2>ClueFL</h2><p>Demonstrates that external knowledge and a well-designed workflow improve file-ranking effectiveness — not a general-purpose repair tool.</p></article></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B24<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s43" data-chapter="Backup / Terminology" data-title="Failure, fault, and repair-location label are not the same thing." data-note="讲述重点｜failure是外部可观测的行为偏差，fault是能导致失败的程序元素/状态，本文任务不是找真正的fault（很难在仓库挖掘研究中观测到），而是用开发者接受的修复所改动的文件作为可观测的repair-location标签。论文特意用repair file而不是ground truth来描述这个标签的解释，只有在正式指标定义里才用ground truth这个词。输出是repository-level、file-granularity的排序列表，可以省略score=0的文件；候选范围刻意不限制在传统源码，只要该构件在目标仓库被维护。

教授可能追问｜那你怎么知道这个文件就是唯一正确的fault位置？

答复依据与边界｜不知道，也不宣称知道；论文明确说label不证明每个改动文件都独立包含根因，也不证明没有其他有效修复方式——这是construct validity威胁里已经承认的边界。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B25: Failure, fault, and repair-location label are not the same thing." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Terminology</div><h1>Failure, fault, and repair-location label are not the same thing.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">FAILURE vs FAULT</span><p>Failure = an externally observed deviation. Fault = a program element/state capable of causing it. The exact fault is rarely observable in a repository-mining study.</p></div><div><span class="label">REPAIR-LOCATION LABEL</span><p>Files modified by the accepted developer fix — an observable proxy, not a proof of the unique causal fault or that no other valid fix exists.</p></div></div><div class="inline-insights"><p><b>Note:</b> "software layer" here means an operational grouping of repository responsibilities — not a neural-network layer.</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B25<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s44" data-chapter="Backup / Evidence regime" data-title=""Execution-free" is stricter than "coverage-free" and more precise than "test-free"." data-note="讲述重点｜execution-free指localizer不编译目标版本、不运行引擎或测试、不做插桩、不注入故障、不收集新的运行时trace，只能拿到清洗后的issue报告和pre-fix仓库快照。issue里可能包含reporter提供的日志、复现步骤或异常栈，这些是报告时就存在的历史证据，不是localization方法自己生成的动态信号。这比coverage-free更严格（coverage-free可能仍需要失败测试输出或crash dump），也比"test-free"这种笼统说法更精确。

教授可能追问｜那论文里出现的堆栈信息算不算作弊利用了执行结果？

答复依据与边界｜不算，因为这些trace是issue reporter在提交时就写在报告里的历史文本，localizer只是读取静态文本，没有自己重新执行目标版本来生成新证据。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B26: "Execution-free" is stricter than "coverage-free" and more precise than "test-free"." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Evidence regime</div><h1>"Execution-free" is stricter than "coverage-free" and more precise than "test-free".</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="challenge-grid"><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">EXECUTION-FREE</span><h2>No new runtime evidence</h2><p>No compile, no run, no instrumentation, no fault injection, no new trace collection on the target revision.</p></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">COVERAGE-FREE ≠ THIS</span><h2>A weaker notion</h2><p>A coverage-free approach may still require a failed-test output, crash dump, or reference run.</p></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">ISSUE-EMBEDDED TRACES OK</span><h2>Historical, not dynamic</h2><p>A stack trace already written in the issue may be read; it was not generated by the localizer executing the old revision.</p></article></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B26<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s45" data-chapter="Backup / Task boundaries" data-title="Not issue localization in general, not repair, not patch-correctness assessment." data-note="讲述重点｜repository issue localization有时泛指为bug、feature request、性能或安全issue找相关代码实体，本文只选bug类issue并评估其观测到的修复位置。自动程序修复(APR)还要生成补丁；像SWE-bench这类基准评估的是通过测试验证的补丁，而不是独立的定位排序。自动补丁正确性评估(APCA，如APPT/RePaCA)则是在已生成补丁之后再判断补丁是否语义正确，既不检索修复文件也不衡量execution-free的文件排序。这些边界防止把修复或补丁分类的准确率误报成定位准确率。

教授可能追问｜那能不能直接拿SWE-bench的结果来对比？

答复依据与边界｜不能直接对比，因为SWE-bench评估的是测试验证过的补丁正确性，衡量的是不同的能力组合（定位+生成变更），协议和输出目标都不同。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B27: Not issue localization in general, not repair, not patch-correctness assessment." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Task boundaries</div><h1>Not issue localization in general, not repair, not patch-correctness assessment.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">NOT REPAIR (APR)</span><p>APR must additionally synthesize a change; SWE-bench-style benchmarks judge a test-validated patch, not an independent localization ranking.</p></div><div><span class="label">NOT PATCH ASSESSMENT (APCA)</span><p>APCA (e.g., APPT, RePaCA) estimates whether an already-generated patch is correct — it neither retrieves a file nor measures execution-free ranking.</p></div></div><div class="inline-insights"><p><b>Why it matters:</b></p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B27<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s46" data-chapter="Backup / Layer-taxonomy construction" data-title="The 8-layer Ollama map is built zero-shot by another LLM, then frozen and reused." data-note="讲述重点｜先从目标仓库抽取package/interface节点清单（Ollama评估快照111个节点），把这份清单交给Claude Opus 4.6，不给标注示例或人工规则，只要求它按功能职责和数据/控制流位置分组。结果是69个节点分到8个命名软件层，其余42个归入3个跨层组。这个taxonomy对Ollama是特定的，但构建流程是可复用的：换一个推理引擎时可以对新仓库重跑同样的清单-分组流程，不需要人工标注数据集，层的数量和名字可能不同。这个map构建一次后原样注入所有评估的issue。

教授可能追问｜用另一个LLM生成taxonomy会不会引入偏差或循环论证？

答复依据与边界｜论文坦诚这是zero-shot程序生成的先验，不是人工验证的黄金标准；它是ClueFL框架自身的构件，在第5章引入，不作为通用背景声称成立；分组质量未做独立正确性验证，只在下游定位效果上间接体现。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B28: The 8-layer Ollama map is built zero-shot by another LLM, then frozen and reused." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Layer-taxonomy construction</div><h1>The 8-layer Ollama map is built zero-shot by another LLM, then frozen and reused.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">HOW IT IS BUILT</span><p>Extract 111 package/interface nodes from Ollama; ask Claude Opus 4.6, with no labeled examples, to group them by functional responsibility and data/control-flow position.</p></div><div><span class="label">RESULT</span><p>69 nodes → 8 named software layers; 42 remaining nodes → 3 cross-cutting groups. Built once, then injected unchanged for every evaluated issue.</p></div></div><div class="inline-insights"><p><b>Reusability:</b> the construction procedure generalizes to other engines; the resulting layer names/boundaries are project-specific and not independently validated as "correct".</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B28<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s47" data-chapter="Backup / Honest gaps this thesis leaves open" data-title="No significance testing, and ClueFL's own cost is not reported." data-note="讲述重点｜两个坦诚的空白：第一，所有比较都是单次归档运行，provider API不暴露可控随机种子，论文没有做显著性检验，报告的差异是描述性观察而非run-to-run方差的估计。第二，第4章详细报告了BugLocator/BLUiR/SWE-agent的interaction步数、token、耗时和美元成本，但第5章的ClueFL对比没有报告ClueFL自身相对baseline增加了多少步数/token/成本——只报告了效果指标。

教授可能追问｜ClueFL会不会效果好是因为烧了更多token/成本换来的？

答复依据与边界｜论文没有提供数据来排除或证实这一点；这是本论文未覆盖的空白，应该作为未来重复运行/效率评估工作的一部分（参见Backup·未来工作）来补充。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B29: No significance testing, and ClueFL's own cost is not reported." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow"></div><h1>No significance testing, and ClueFL's own cost is not reported.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="challenge-grid"><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">NO SIGNIFICANCE TESTS</span><h2>Single archived run per config</h2><p>No controllable random seed is exposed by the provider APIs; reported differences are descriptive, not variance estimates.</p></article><article class="fl-card"><span class="label">CLUEFL COST UNREPORTED</span><h2>Effectiveness only</h2><p>Chapter 4 reports steps/tokens/cost for the RQ1 baselines; Chapter 5 does not report ClueFL's own steps, tokens, or dollar cost relative to the SWE-agent baseline.</p></article></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B29<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s48" data-chapter="Backup / Qualitative methodology" data-title="Manual trajectory coding is illustrative, not an inter-rater-validated protocol." data-note="讲述重点｜RQ3和RQ4的失败/成功机制分析都来自作者手工阅读agent的完整交互trajectory（仓库检查、工具调用、最终排序），逐案例识别证据不可达、因果链截断、非源码构件欠检查等模式，并挑选具体案例（如Case 107/126/86、PR13445/6905/5121）来说明每种机制。论文没有报告多名标注者独立编码后的一致性系数（如Cohen's kappa），也没有对所有145×2个trajectory做穷尽式编码。

教授可能追问｜这些失败机制的分类会不会是作者主观挑选出来支持论点的案例？

答复依据与边界｜这是合理的担忧；论文将这些模式作为从观察到的trajectory中识别出的"recurring, identifiable pitfalls"，用具体案例做说明性证据，而非声称经过独立编码验证的详尽统计——严格的观察者间信度检验留作未来工作。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B30: Manual trajectory coding is illustrative, not an inter-rater-validated protocol." tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Qualitative methodology</div><h1>Manual trajectory coding is illustrative, not an inter-rater-validated protocol.</h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">WHAT WAS DONE</span><p>Single-author manual reading of complete agent trajectories (repository actions, tool calls, final rankings) to identify recurring failure/success mechanisms, illustrated with concrete PR cases.</p></div><div><span class="label">WHAT WAS NOT DONE</span><p>No multi-coder inter-rater reliability score (e.g., Cohen's kappa); not an exhaustive coding of every one of the 145×2 trajectories.</p></div></div><div class="inline-insights"><p><b>Framing:</b> patterns are presented as illustrative, recurring pitfalls grounded in specific cases — not a statistically validated taxonomy.</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B30<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section><section class="slide " id="s49" data-chapter="Backup / Reproducibility artifacts" data-title="What is actually released alongside the thesis?" data-note="讲述重点｜145例的Ollama评估数据集（清洗后的issue、pre-fix版本号、修复位置标签及元数据）公开在GitHub仓库；复现包里还包含精确的任务指令、模型标识符、生效运行设置、完整输出和trajectory存档，供审计用。检索方法是确定性的，只跑一次；agent方法因为成本高，同样只保留单次归档运行，但完整trajectory都存档以便审查。

教授可能追问｜第三方能不能完全复现你的ClueFL数字？

答复依据与边界｜数据集和baseline的复现材料是公开的；ClueFL的具体prompt/配置在附录A.1中提供，但由于provider API不暴露随机种子、且各配置只有单次归档运行，完全逐位复现相同排序不能保证，只能复现同一协议下的可比较实验。" data-backup="true" aria-label="B31: What is actually released alongside the thesis?" tabindex="-1">
<div class="slide-top"><span>TECHNICAL UNIVERSITY OF MUNICH <i>/</i> CHAIR OF SOFTWARE ENGINEERING &amp; AI</span><img class="tum-wordmark" src="images/tum_logo.png" alt="TUM"></div>
<header class="slide-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Backup / Reproducibility artifacts</div><h1></h1></header>
<div class="slide-body"><div class="protocol-notes"><div><span class="label">PUBLIC OLLAMAFLBENCH</span><p>145 cleaned issues, pre-fix revision identifiers, repair-location labels, and metadata at github.com/tianhaogutum/OllamaFLBench.</p></div><div><span class="label">REPLICATION PACKAGE</span><p>Exact task instructions, model identifiers, effective run settings, outputs, and archived trajectories for audit.</p></div></div><div class="inline-insights"><p><b>Caveat:</b> no controllable random seed and one archived run per configuration, so bit-identical reproduction of stochastic agent rankings is not guaranteed.</p></div></div>
<footer class="slide-footer"><span>BACKUP · B31<span class="footer-total"> / 31</span></span></footer>
</section></div></div></main>
<footer class="app-footer"><nav class="chapters" aria-label="Presentation chapters"><button class="chapter-button" data-go="0">Background</button><button class="chapter-button" data-go="9">RQ1 · Feasibility</button><button class="chapter-button" data-go="14">RQ2 · Failures</button><button class="chapter-button" data-go="22">RQ3 · ClueFL</button><button class="chapter-button" data-go="27">Conclusion</button><button class="chapter-button" data-go="29">Backup</button></nav><div class="nav-controls"><button id="prev" class="nav-arrow" aria-label="Previous slide"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m14 6-6 6 6 6"/></svg></button><span id="page-count" class="page-count"></span><button id="next" class="nav-arrow" aria-label="Next slide"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m10 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg></button></div></footer>
<div id="progress" class="global-progress" aria-hidden="true"></div><div id="announcement" class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></div>
<aside id="notes" class="notes-panel" aria-label="Speaker notes" hidden><div class="notes-title"><h2 id="notes-number">Speaker notes</h2><button id="notes-close" aria-label="Close speaker notes">×</button></div><p id="notes-copy" lang="zh-CN"></p></aside>
<dialog id="overview" aria-labelledby="overview-title"><div class="dialog-header"><h2 id="overview-title">Presentation overview <small>· 20 slides + 31 backup</small></h2><button class="dialog-close" data-close="overview" aria-label="Close overview">×</button></div><div id="overview-grid" class="overview-grid"></div></dialog>
<dialog id="figure-dialog" aria-labelledby="figure-title"><div class="dialog-header"><h2 id="figure-title"></h2><button class="dialog-close" data-close="figure-dialog" aria-label="Close enlarged figure">×</button></div><img id="figure-image" alt=""><a id="figure-source" target="_blank" rel="noopener"></a></dialog>
<dialog id="help-dialog" aria-labelledby="help-title"><div class="dialog-header"><h2 id="help-title">Presentation shortcuts</h2><button class="dialog-close" data-close="help-dialog" aria-label="Close shortcuts">×</button></div><dl><dt>← / →</dt><dd>Previous / next slide</dd><dt>Space / Shift Space</dt><dd>Next / previous slide</dd><dt>Home / End</dt><dd>First / last main slide</dd><dt>O</dt><dd>Slide overview + backup</dd><dt>N</dt><dd>Chinese speaker notes</dd><dt>F</dt><dd>Fullscreen presentation</dd><dt>Esc</dt><dd>Close a dialog or notes</dd><dt>Click a figure</dt><dd></dd></dl><p style="font-size:13px;margin-top:20px">Print exports the 16 main slides. On touch screens, swipe left or right to navigate.</p></dialog>
<div id="toast" class="toast" role="status" hidden></div>
<noscript><style>.slide:first-child{display:flex}.stage{transform:scale(.7);transform-origin:top left}</style><p>This presentation needs JavaScript for navigation. Please enable JavaScript to view all slides.</p></noscript>
<script>
'use strict';
(() => {
 const slides = [...document.querySelectorAll('.slide')];
 const totalMain = slides.filter(s => !s.dataset.backup).length;
 const stageWrap = document.querySelector('.stage-wrap');
 const viewport = document.querySelector('.viewport');
 const prev = document.querySelector('#prev');
 const next = document.querySelector('#next');
 const overview = document.querySelector('#overview');
 const figureDialog = document.querySelector('#figure-dialog');
 const helpDialog = document.querySelector('#help-dialog');
 const notes = document.querySelector('#notes');
 const notesButton = document.querySelector('#notes-toggle');
 let current = 0;
 let touch = null;
 let toastTimeout;
 const hashIndex = () => {
  const hash = location.hash || '';
  const match = hash.match(/^#s(.+)$/);
  if (!match) return 0;
  const requestedId = `s${match[1]}`;
  const exactIndex = slides.findIndex(slide => slide.id === requestedId);
  if (exactIndex >= 0) return exactIndex;
  const numericIndex = Number(match[1]);
  if (Number.isFinite(numericIndex)) {
   return Math.max(0, Math.min(slides.length - 1, numericIndex - 1));
  }
  return 0;
};
function fit() {
  const style = getComputedStyle(viewport);
  const w = viewport.clientWidth - parseFloat(style.paddingLeft) - parseFloat(style.paddingRight);
  const h = viewport.clientHeight - parseFloat(style.paddingTop) - parseFloat(style.paddingBottom);
  const scale = Math.max(.05, Math.min(w / 1440, h / 810));
  document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--stage-scale', scale);
  stageWrap.style.width = `${1440 * scale}px`;
  stageWrap.style.height = `${810 * scale}px`;
 }
 function go(index, updateHash = true) {
  const candidate = Number(index);
  if (!Number.isFinite(candidate)) return;
  current = Math.max(0, Math.min(slides.length - 1, Math.trunc(candidate)));
  const previousActive = document.activeElement;
  const shouldRestoreFocus = previousActive?.closest('.slide') && previousActive.closest('.slide') !== slides[current];
  slides.forEach((slide, i) => {
   const active = i === current;
   slide.classList.toggle('active', active);
   slide.setAttribute('aria-hidden', String(!active));
   slide.inert = !active;
  });
  if (shouldRestoreFocus) slides[current].focus({preventScroll:true});
  const backup = current >= totalMain;
  document.querySelector('#page-count').innerHTML = backup ? `<strong>B${String(current - totalMain + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</strong> / 05` : `<strong>${String(current + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</strong> / ${totalMain}`;
  document.querySelector('#progress').style.width = `${Math.min(current + 1, totalMain) / totalMain * 100}%`;
  prev.disabled = current === 0;
  next.disabled = current === slides.length - 1;
  next.setAttribute('aria-label', current === totalMain - 1 ? 'Open backup slides' : 'Next slide');
  document.querySelector('#notes-copy').textContent = slides[current].dataset.note;
  const seconds = Number(slides[current].dataset.seconds || 0);
  const duration = seconds ? ` · ${Math.floor(seconds / 60)}:${String(seconds % 60).padStart(2, '0')} suggested` : '';
  document.querySelector('#notes-number').textContent = `Speaker notes · ${backup ? 'Backup ' + (current - totalMain + 1) : current + 1}${duration}`;
  document.querySelector('#announcement').textContent = `Slide ${current + 1} of ${slides.length}. ${slides[current].dataset.title}`;
  document.querySelectorAll('.chapter-button').forEach((button, i, all) => {
   const start = Number(button.dataset.go);
   const end = i + 1 < all.length ? Number(all[i + 1].dataset.go) : slides.length;
   const active = current >= start && current < end;
   button.classList.toggle('active', active);
   if (active) button.setAttribute('aria-current', 'step'); else button.removeAttribute('aria-current');
  });
  document.querySelectorAll('.overview-item').forEach((button, i) =>< 0 ? 1 : -1);
 }, {passive:true});
 viewport.addEventListener('touchcancel', () => {touch = null;}, {passive:true});
 window.addEventListener('hashchange', () => { go(hashIndex(), false); showAllFragments(slides[current]); });
 window.addEventListener('resize', fit);
 document.addEventListener('fullscreenchange', () => {
  document.querySelector('#fullscreen-toggle').setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(Boolean(document.fullscreenElement)));
  fit();
 });
 new ResizeObserver(fit).observe(viewport);
 go(hashIndex()); showAllFragments(slides[current]); fit();
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
